# slug: ch19-unroll
# source: chapters/ch19.tex:58 (approximate line of \begin{algorithm})
# caption: Unrolling a counted loop with a cleanup loop
# label: alg:ch19-unroll
# require: counted loop L, nonnegative exact trip count T, step 1, integer factor k >= 1, safe counter arithmetic
# ensure: body replicated k times plus a loop for the remainder
# keywords: INPUT/OUTPUT/REQUIRE/ENSURE/FOR/FORALL/WHILE/IF/ELSE/RETURN

REQUIRE counted loop L, nonnegative exact trip count T, step 1, integer factor k >= 1, safe counter arithmetic
ENSURE body replicated k times plus a loop for the remainder
full <- floor(T / k)
rem <- T mod k
rewrite L to iterate full times with step k and k body copies
adjust each copy j to use index i + j for 0 <= j < k
emit a cleanup loop of rem single copies after L
run verification that full * k + rem = T

